---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
const matrix = [[2, 0, 0], [1, 3, 0], [4, -1, 0.5]];
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Jacobian structure"
  title="Triangular structure makes the determinant cheap"
  caption="Reconstructed from the triangular-matrix and Jacobian discussion on pages 34–35, with an exact editorial example. Here f is linear and Jf = [[2,0,0],[1,3,0],[4,−1,0.5]]. The dependency graph explains the zeros above the diagonal: output i only uses inputs 1 through i. Its determinant is the diagonal product 3. For nonlinear maps, a Jacobian describes local first-order geometry; multiplying already available diagonal entries costs O(d), while obtaining them may require additional computation."
>
  <div class="jacobian-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 445" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-jacobian-matrix-title flow-jacobian-matrix-desc">
      <title id="flow-jacobian-matrix-title">Compute a triangular determinant from its diagonal</title>
      <desc id="flow-jacobian-matrix-desc">A three by three lower triangular Jacobian has rows two zero zero, one three zero, and four minus one zero point five. The diagonal entries are highlighted. Their product is three, so the natural log of the absolute determinant is log three. This linear map multiplies volume by three and divides density by three.</desc>
      <text x="160" y="27" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">A lower-triangular Jacobian</text>
      <text x="160" y="52" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Entry (i, j) = ∂xᵢ / ∂zⱼ</text>
      {[0, 1, 2].map((j) => <text x={96 + j * 68} y="94" text-anchor="middle" class="coordinate">{`z${['₁', '₂', '₃'][j]}`}</text>)}
      {[0, 1, 2].map((i) => <text x="30" y={153 + i * 65} text-anchor="middle" class="coordinate">{`x${['₁', '₂', '₃'][i]}`}</text>)}
      <path d="M 65 116 H 55 V 293 H 65 M 263 116 H 273 V 293 H 263" class="bracket" />
      {matrix.map((row, i) => row.map((value, j) => (
        <g>
          {i === j && <rect x={72 + j * 68} y={126 + i * 65} width="48" height="42" rx="4" class="diagonal-cell" />}
          <text x={96 + j * 68} y={154 + i * 65} text-anchor="middle" class:list={['entry', { diagonal: i === j, zero: j > i }]}>{value}</text>
        </g>
      )))}
      <path d="M 96 177 L 151 211 M 175 238 L 221 270" class="diagonal-guide" />
      <text x="160" y="331" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">det Jf = 2 · 3 · 0.5 = 3</text>
      <text x="160" y="362" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">log |det Jf| = ln 3</text>
      <text x="160" y="410" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Volume ×3; density ÷3</text>
      <text x="160" y="434" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">Only diagonal entries enter the product</text>
    </svg>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 320 445" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-jacobian-dependencies-title flow-jacobian-dependencies-desc">
      <title id="flow-jacobian-dependencies-title">Ordered dependencies produce a triangular Jacobian</title>
      <desc id="flow-jacobian-dependencies-desc">Three input nodes z1, z2, and z3 connect to output nodes x1, x2, and x3. z1 affects all outputs; z2 affects x2 and x3; z3 affects only x3. The exact equations are x1 equals two z1; x2 equals z1 plus three z2; x3 equals four z1 minus z2 plus one half z3.</desc>
      <defs><marker id="flow-jacobian-active-head" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="active-head" /></marker><marker id="flow-jacobian-diagonal-head" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="diagonal-head" /></marker></defs>
      <text x="160" y="27" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Order the dependencies</text>
      <text x="160" y="52" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">xᵢ only depends on z₁, …, zᵢ</text>
      <text x="60" y="83" text-anchor="middle" class="coordinate">Inputs</text><text x="260" y="83" text-anchor="middle" class="coordinate">Outputs</text>
      <g class="active-edge" marker-end="url(#flow-jacobian-active-head)"><path d="M 82 114 L 236 186" /><path d="M 82 114 L 236 258" /><path d="M 82 186 L 236 258" /></g>
      <g class="diagonal-edge" marker-end="url(#flow-jacobian-diagonal-head)"><path d="M 84 114 H 236" /><path d="M 84 186 H 236" /><path d="M 84 258 H 236" /></g>
      {[0, 1, 2].map((i) => (
        <g>
          <circle cx="60" cy={114 + i * 72} r="19" class="node" /><circle cx="260" cy={114 + i * 72} r="19" class="node" />
          <text x="60" y={120 + i * 72} text-anchor="middle">{`z${['₁', '₂', '₃'][i]}`}</text><text x="260" y={120 + i * 72} text-anchor="middle">{`x${['₁', '₂', '₃'][i]}`}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <text x="160" y="307" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Missing edges give the upper zeros</text>
      <text x="160" y="345" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">x₁ = 2z₁</text>
      <text x="160" y="376" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">x₂ = z₁ + 3z₂</text>
      <text x="160" y="407" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">x₃ = 4z₁ − z₂ + 0.5z₃</text>
      <text x="160" y="434" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">Diagonal edges set the volume factor</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .jacobian-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 380px; margin-inline: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16px; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  .muted, .coordinate { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .accent { fill: var(--accent); font-size: 13px; }
  .formula { font-size: 17px; }
  .entry { font-size: 23px; }
  .diagonal { fill: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  .zero { fill: var(--muted); }
  .diagonal-cell { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .bracket { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.7; }
  .diagonal-guide { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; }
  .active-edge, .active-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .diagonal-edge, .diagonal-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.7; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .node { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .jacobian-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; } }
</style>
